.Dd November 11, 2026
.Dt HANDLE_CLOSE 2
.Os RavenBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm handle_close
.Nd close a handle
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Ft int
.Fn handle_close "Handle handle"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The .Nm system call closes .Fa handle in the caller's handle table.
.Pp
A handle packs a 24-bit table index and an 8-bit generation. A successful close increments the
generation, so every earlier handle value for that slot fails with
.Er EBADF .
When the closing generation is 255 the slot is retired instead of wrapping to generation 0: the
slot is never reused and stale handles stay invalid permanently.
.Pp
Closing also removes .Fa handle from the caller's event-queue registrations, but only after the
close commits. A close that fails, for example with a stale generation, leaves every registration
intact.
.Pp
This page documents the native RavenBSD ABI; see the
.Pa raven-abi
crate for the exact numeric value and types.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
On success .Nm returns a non-negative value; on failure it returns a negative error number.
.Sh STANDARDS
RavenBSD ABI v1.
